<title>UK: India seen raising sugar exports in 1996/97 -Licht.</title>
<headline>India seen raising sugar exports in 1996/97 -Licht.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>India is likely to increase its sugar exports to the free market in the 1996/97 crop year (September/August) and reduce its massive share of world stocks, statistician F.O. Licht said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The fact that India's share of the stocks is expected to fall to 43 percent indicates a build-up in other areas,&quot; Licht said in its first estimate of the 1996/97 sugar balance.</p>
<p>&quot;That could have a sharp impact on prices, as the holders of this sugar would probably not wish to hold it off the market.&quot;</p>
<p>It gave no figure for India's current share of world sugar stocks.</p>
<p>&quot;It also seems likely that exports from India will also rise during 1996/97, if markets can be found,&quot; Licht said.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
</text>
